Let the Matroska demuxer take its chapters from the default edition alone.

A Matroska file can carry several editions, each with its own chapters, such as a theatrical and an
extended cut, and RFC 9559 says a player uses the default one: the first edition flagged
EditionFlagDefault, or the first edition when none is (section 20.1.2). It also says a hidden
chapter is not shown, that the content of a disabled chapter is skipped, and that a chapter with a
ChapterSegmentUUID plays a range of another segment, so its times are that segment's.

The demuxer parsed every edition's ChapterAtoms into one list and skipped all three flags and the
link, then made a chapter of each entry that started later than the last one it kept. A file with
two editions therefore listed the first edition's chapters followed by any of the second's that
started later, hidden and disabled chapters included, and a chapter of another file at a time that
means nothing in this one; stream discovery then ended a chapter where the other edition's next one
started.

The chapters are now kept per edition, and the chapter list comes from the default edition alone,
without the chapters that are hidden, disabled, or linked to another segment. The segment's own
SegmentUUID is read so that a link naming it, which the specification forbids, still counts as this
segment. A file with one edition and none of those flags reads exactly as before, and tags that
target a chapter still find it whichever edition it is in. Nested chapters are still not read.

Applied by BuildFFmpegTask before configure, after 0006, whose syntax table sizes it shares a line
with. Fixes yuroyami/KiteFFmpeg#172.

